				<div id="bodyContent" class="vector-body" aria-labelledby="firstHeading" data-mw-ve-target-container>
					<div class="vector-body-before-content">
							<div class="mw-indicators">
		</div>

						<div id="siteSub" class="noprint">From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia</div>
					</div>
					<div id="contentSub"><div id="mw-content-subtitle"><div class="cdx-message--warning mw-revision cdx-message cdx-message--block" aria-live="polite"><span class="cdx-message__icon"></span><div class="cdx-message__content"><div id="mw-revision-info-current"><b>This is the <a href="/wiki/Help:Page_history" title="Help:Page history">current revision</a> of this page, as edited by <span id="mw-revision-name"><a href="/wiki/User:Maruko-chan_2026" class="mw-userlink" title="User:Maruko-chan 2026" data-mw-revid="1363651720"><bdi>Maruko-chan 2026</bdi></a> <span class="mw-usertoollinks">(<a href="/wiki/User_talk:Maruko-chan_2026" class="mw-usertoollinks-talk" title="User talk:Maruko-chan 2026">talk</a> | <a href="/wiki/Special:Contributions/Maruko-chan_2026" class="mw-usertoollinks-contribs" title="Special:Contributions/Maruko-chan 2026">contribs</a>)</span></span> at <span id="mw-revision-date">13:43, 11 July 2026</span><span id="mw-revision-summary"> <span class="comment">(Link suggestions feature: 3 links added.)</span></span>. The present address (URL) is a <a href="/wiki/Help:Permanent_link" title="Help:Permanent link">permanent link</a> to this version.</b><span id="revision-info-current-plain" style="display: none;">Revision as of 13:43, 11 July 2026 by <a href="/wiki/User:Maruko-chan_2026" class="mw-userlink" title="User:Maruko-chan 2026" data-mw-revid="1363651720"><bdi>Maruko-chan 2026</bdi></a> <span class="mw-usertoollinks">(<a href="/wiki/User_talk:Maruko-chan_2026" class="mw-usertoollinks-talk" title="User talk:Maruko-chan 2026">talk</a> | <a href="/wiki/Special:Contributions/Maruko-chan_2026" class="mw-usertoollinks-contribs" title="Special:Contributions/Maruko-chan 2026">contribs</a>)</span> <span class="comment">(Link suggestions feature: 3 links added.)</span></span></div><div id="mw-revision-nav">(<a href="/w/index.php?title=Borel%E2%80%93Moore_homology&amp;diff=prev&amp;oldid=1363651720" title="Borel–Moore homology">diff</a>) <a href="/w/index.php?title=Borel%E2%80%93Moore_homology&amp;direction=prev&amp;oldid=1363651720" title="Borel–Moore homology">← Previous revision</a> | Latest revision (diff) | Newer revision → (diff)</div></div></div></div></div>
					
					
					<div id="mw-content-text" class="mw-body-content"><div class="mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output" lang="en" dir="ltr" data-mw-parsoid-version="0.24.0.0-alpha18" data-mw-html-version="2.8.0"><section data-mw-section-id="0" id="mwAQ"><div class="shortdescription nomobile noexcerpt noprint searchaux" style="display:none" about="#mwt1" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Short description","href":"./Template:Short_description"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Homology theory for locally compact spaces"}},"i":0}}]}'>Homology theory for locally compact spaces</div><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_short_description"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Short_description_matches_Wikidata"/></span>
<p id="mwAw">In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Topology" title="Topology" id="mwBA">topology</a>, <b id="mwBQ">Borel−Moore homology</b> or <b id="mwBg">homology with closed support</b> is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Homology_theory" title="Homology theory" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBw">homology theory</a> for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Locally_compact_space" title="Locally compact space" id="mwCA">locally compact spaces</a>, introduced by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armand_Borel" title="Armand Borel" id="mwCQ">Armand Borel</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Coleman_Moore" title="John Coleman Moore" id="mwCg">John Moore</a> in 1960.<sup about="#mwt2" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBorelMoore1960_1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"","name":"FOOTNOTEBorelMoore1960"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBorelMoore1960-1"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sfn","href":"./Template:Sfn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Borel"},"2":{"wt":"Moore"},"3":{"wt":"1960"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBorelMoore1960-1" id="mwCw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQ">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDw">For reasonable <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compact_space" title="Compact space" id="mwEA">compact spaces</a>, Borel−Moore homology coincides with the usual <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singular_homology" title="Singular homology" id="mwEQ">singular homology</a>. For non-compact spaces, each theory has its own advantages. In particular, a closed oriented <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Submanifold" title="Submanifold" id="mwEg">submanifold</a> defines a class in Borel–Moore homology, but not in ordinary homology unless the submanifold is compact.</p>

<p id="mwEw">Note: Borel <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equivariant_cohomology" title="Equivariant cohomology" id="mwFA">equivariant cohomology</a> is an invariant of spaces with an action of a group <i id="mwFQ">G</i>; it is defined as <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt5" id="mwFg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H^*_G(X) = H^*((EG \\times X)/G)."}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{G}^{*}(X)=H^{*}((EG\times X)/G).}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msubsup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>G</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo>∗<!-- ∗ --></mo>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <msup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo>∗<!-- ∗ --></mo>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>E</mi>
        <mi>G</mi>
        <mo>×<!-- × --></mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mo>/</mo>
        </mrow>
        <mi>G</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>.</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H_{G}^{*}(X)=H^{*}((EG\times X)/G).}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/c9807b39c0deadcb12f9e1bec2288a774f3cbd51" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.005ex; width:29.178ex; height:3.009ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{G}^{*}(X)=H^{*}((EG\times X)/G).}"/></span> That is not related to the subject of this article.</p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" id="mwFw" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}'/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwGA" aria-labelledby="Definition"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Definition">Definition</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Borel%E2%80%93Moore_homology&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: Definition"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwGQ">There are several ways to define Borel−Moore homology. They all coincide for reasonable spaces such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manifold" title="Manifold" id="mwGg">manifolds</a> and locally finite <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CW_complexes" title="CW complexes" class="mw-redirect" id="mwGw">CW complexes</a>.</p>

<section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwHA" aria-labelledby="Definition_via_sheaf_cohomology"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Definition_via_sheaf_cohomology">Definition via sheaf cohomology</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Borel%E2%80%93Moore_homology&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: Definition via sheaf cohomology"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwHQ">For any locally compact space <i id="mwHg">X</i>, Borel–Moore homology with integral coefficients is defined as the cohomology of the dual of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chain_complex" title="Chain complex" id="mwHw">chain complex</a> which computes <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sheaf_cohomology" title="Sheaf cohomology" id="mwIA">sheaf cohomology</a> with compact support.<sup about="#mwt6" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-2" id="mwIQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwIg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIw">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJA">]</span></span></a></sup> As a result, there is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Short_exact_sequence" title="Short exact sequence" class="mw-redirect" id="mwJQ">short exact sequence</a> analogous to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Universal_coefficient_theorem" title="Universal coefficient theorem" id="mwJg">universal coefficient theorem</a>:</p>

<p id="mwJw"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-block" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt7" id="mwKA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{"display":"block"},"body":{"extsrc":"0 \\to \\text{Ext}^1_{\\Z}(H^{i+1}_c(X,\\Z),\\Z) \\to H_i^{BM}(X,\\Z) \\to \\text{Hom}(H^i_c(X,\\Z),\\Z) \\to 0."}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-display mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="{\displaystyle 0\to {\text{Ext}}_{\mathbb {Z} }^{1}(H_{c}^{i+1}(X,\mathbb {Z} ),\mathbb {Z} )\to H_{i}^{BM}(X,\mathbb {Z} )\to {\text{Hom}}(H_{c}^{i}(X,\mathbb {Z} ),\mathbb {Z} )\to 0.}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mn>0</mn>
        <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
