        <mn>0.</mn>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle 0\to {\text{Ext}}_{\mathbb {Z} }^{1}(H_{c}^{i+1}(X,\mathbb {Z} ),\mathbb {Z} )\to H_{i}^{BM}(X,\mathbb {Z} )\to {\text{Hom}}(H_{c}^{i}(X,\mathbb {Z} ),\mathbb {Z} )\to 0.}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/f164a3ee25a2992d9fd0b3cbf782a3001e153970" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-display mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.005ex; width:68.438ex; height:3.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle 0\to {\text{Ext}}_{\mathbb {Z} }^{1}(H_{c}^{i+1}(X,\mathbb {Z} ),\mathbb {Z} )\to H_{i}^{BM}(X,\mathbb {Z} )\to {\text{Hom}}(H_{c}^{i}(X,\mathbb {Z} ),\mathbb {Z} )\to 0.}"/></span></p>

<p id="mwKQ">In what follows, the coefficients <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt8" id="mwKg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\Z"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {Z} }">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Z</mi>
        </mrow>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {Z} }</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/449494a083e0a1fda2b61c62b2f09b6bee4633dc" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.55ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {Z} }"/></span> are not written.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwKw" aria-labelledby="Definition_via_locally_finite_chains"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Definition_via_locally_finite_chains">Definition via locally finite chains</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Borel%E2%80%93Moore_homology&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: Definition via locally finite chains"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwLA">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singular_homology" title="Singular homology" id="mwLQ">singular homology</a> of a topological space <i id="mwLg">X</i> is defined as the homology of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chain_complex" title="Chain complex" id="mwLw">chain complex</a> of singular chains, that is, finite linear combinations of continuous maps from the simplex to <i id="mwMA">X</i>. The Borel−Moore homology of a reasonable locally compact space <i id="mwMQ">X</i>, on the other hand, is isomorphic to the homology of the chain complex of <b id="mwMg">locally finite</b> singular chains. Here "reasonable" means <i id="mwMw">X</i> is locally contractible, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Σ-compact" title="Σ-compact" class="mw-redirect" id="mwNA">σ-compact</a>, and of finite dimension.<sup about="#mwt9" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-3" id="mwNQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwNg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNw">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwOQ">In more detail, let <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt10" id="mwOg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"C_i^{BM}(X)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle C_{i}^{BM}(X)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msubsup>
          <mi>C</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle C_{i}^{BM}(X)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/be44b469bb2edfec5520e77d9c8f7ca71fd03880" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.005ex; width:8.794ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle C_{i}^{BM}(X)}"/></span> be the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abelian_group" title="Abelian group" id="mwOw">abelian group</a> of formal (infinite) sums</p>

<p id="mwPA"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-block" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt11" id="mwPQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{"display":"block"},"body":{"extsrc":" u = \\sum_{\\sigma} a_{\\sigma } \\sigma, "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-display mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="{\displaystyle u=\sum _{\sigma }a_{\sigma }\sigma ,}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>u</mi>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <munder>
          <mo>∑<!-- ∑ --></mo>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>σ<!-- σ --></mi>
          </mrow>
        </munder>
        <msub>
          <mi>a</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>σ<!-- σ --></mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mi>σ<!-- σ --></mi>
        <mo>,</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle u=\sum _{\sigma }a_{\sigma }\sigma ,}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/56ca105c6c471a4c86e17b698cdbf70900926c9d" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-display mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -3.005ex; width:12.549ex; height:5.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle u=\sum _{\sigma }a_{\sigma }\sigma ,}"/></span></p>

<p id="mwPg">where <i id="mwPw">σ</i> runs over the set of all continuous maps from the standard <i id="mwQA">i</i>-simplex Δ<sup id="mwQQ"><i id="mwQg">i</i></sup> to <i id="mwQw">X</i> and each <i id="mwRA">a<sub id="mwRQ">σ</sub></i> is an integer, such that for each compact subset <i id="mwRg">K</i> of <i id="mwRw">X</i>, we have  <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt12" id="mwSA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"a_\\sigma\\neq 0"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle a_{\sigma }\neq 0}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>a</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>σ<!-- σ --></mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo>≠<!-- ≠ --></mo>
        <mn>0</mn>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle a_{\sigma }\neq 0}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/71f5bc21fbfb94c4354b2fb1ad2b22faf6b57fd9" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:6.663ex; height:2.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle a_{\sigma }\neq 0}"/></span> for only finitely many <i id="mwSQ">σ</i> whose image meets <i id="mwSg">K</i>. Then the usual definition of the boundary ∂ of a singular chain makes these abelian groups into a chain complex:</p>

<p id="mwSw"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-block" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt13" id="mwTA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{"display":"block"},"body":{"extsrc":" \\cdots \\to C_2^{BM}(X) \\to C_1^{BM}(X) \\to C_0^{BM}(X) \\to 0."}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-display mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="{\displaystyle \cdots \to C_{2}^{BM}(X)\to C_{1}^{BM}(X)\to C_{0}^{BM}(X)\to 0.}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mo>⋯<!-- ⋯ --></mo>
        <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
        <msubsup>
          <mi>C</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>2</mn>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
        <msubsup>
          <mi>C</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>1</mn>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
        <msubsup>
          <mi>C</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>0</mn>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
        <mn>0.</mn>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \cdots \to C_{2}^{BM}(X)\to C_{1}^{BM}(X)\to C_{0}^{BM}(X)\to 0.}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/6fc4272205e55202c3e318c225add019f0c07018" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-display mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.005ex; width:45.37ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \cdots \to C_{2}^{BM}(X)\to C_{1}^{BM}(X)\to C_{0}^{BM}(X)\to 0.}"/></span></p>

<p id="mwTQ">The Borel−Moore homology groups <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt14" id="mwTg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H_i^{BM}(X)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msubsup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/218e23a871d1bc5daea15afd41c615d42afcbd5f" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.005ex; width:9.099ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)}"/></span> are the homology groups of this chain complex. That is,</p>

<p id="mwTw"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-block" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt15" id="mwUA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{"display":"block"},"body":{"extsrc":"H^{BM}_i (X) = \\ker \\left (\\partial : C_i^{BM}(X) \\to C_{i-1}^{BM}(X) \\right )/ \\text{im} \\left (\\partial :C_{i+1}^{BM}(X) \\to C_i^{BM}(X) \\right ). "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-display mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)=\ker \left(\partial :C_{i}^{BM}(X)\to C_{i-1}^{BM}(X)\right)/{\text{im}}\left(\partial :C_{i+1}^{BM}(X)\to C_{i}^{BM}(X)\right).}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msubsup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <mi>ker</mi>
        <mo>⁡<!-- ⁡ --></mo>
        <mrow>
          <mo>(</mo>
          <mrow>
            <mi mathvariant="normal">∂<!-- ∂ --></mi>
            <mo>:</mo>
            <msubsup>
              <mi>C</mi>
              <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
                <mi>i</mi>
              </mrow>
              <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
                <mi>B</mi>
                <mi>M</mi>
              </mrow>
            </msubsup>
            <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
            <mi>X</mi>
            <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
            <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
            <msubsup>
              <mi>C</mi>
              <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
                <mi>i</mi>
                <mo>−<!-- − --></mo>
                <mn>1</mn>
              </mrow>
              <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
                <mi>B</mi>
                <mi>M</mi>
              </mrow>
            </msubsup>
            <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
            <mi>X</mi>
            <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
          </mrow>
          <mo>)</mo>
        </mrow>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mo>/</mo>
        </mrow>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mtext>im</mtext>
        </mrow>
        <mrow>
          <mo>(</mo>
          <mrow>
            <mi mathvariant="normal">∂<!-- ∂ --></mi>
            <mo>:</mo>
            <msubsup>
              <mi>C</mi>
              <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
                <mi>i</mi>
                <mo>+</mo>
                <mn>1</mn>
              </mrow>
              <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
                <mi>B</mi>
                <mi>M</mi>
              </mrow>
            </msubsup>
            <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
            <mi>X</mi>
            <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
            <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
            <msubsup>
              <mi>C</mi>
              <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
                <mi>i</mi>
              </mrow>
              <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
                <mi>B</mi>
                <mi>M</mi>
              </mrow>
            </msubsup>
            <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
            <mi>X</mi>
            <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
          </mrow>
          <mo>)</mo>
        </mrow>
        <mo>.</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)=\ker \left(\partial :C_{i}^{BM}(X)\to C_{i-1}^{BM}(X)\right)/{\text{im}}\left(\partial :C_{i+1}^{BM}(X)\to C_{i}^{BM}(X)\right).}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/75d65def8237356f0fe6d4b68b8c416f49e235b1" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-display mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.171ex; width:73.708ex; height:3.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)=\ker \left(\partial :C_{i}^{BM}(X)\to C_{i-1}^{BM}(X)\right)/{\text{im}}\left(\partial :C_{i+1}^{BM}(X)\to C_{i}^{BM}(X)\right).}"/></span></p>

<p id="mwUQ">If <i id="mwUg">X</i> is compact, then every locally finite chain is in fact finite. So, given that <i id="mwUw">X</i> is "reasonable" in the sense above, Borel−Moore homology <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt16" id="mwVA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H_i^{BM}(X)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msubsup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/218e23a871d1bc5daea15afd41c615d42afcbd5f" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.005ex; width:9.099ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)}"/></span> coincides with the usual singular homology <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt17" id="mwVQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H_i(X)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{i}(X)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msub>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H_{i}(X)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/7b27c0beeb0ee4abaf21504ce7c4c32dd91e290e" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:6.52ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{i}(X)}"/></span> for <i id="mwVg">X</i> compact.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mwVw" aria-labelledby="Definition_via_compactifications"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Definition_via_compactifications">Definition via compactifications</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Borel%E2%80%93Moore_homology&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4" title="Edit section: Definition via compactifications"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwWA">Suppose that <i id="mwWQ">X</i> is homeomorphic to the complement of a closed subcomplex <i id="mwWg">S</i> in a finite CW complex <i id="mwWw">Y</i>. Then Borel–Moore homology <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt18" id="mwXA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H_i^{BM}(X)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msubsup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/218e23a871d1bc5daea15afd41c615d42afcbd5f" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.005ex; width:9.099ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)}"/></span> is isomorphic to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Relative_homology" title="Relative homology" id="mwXQ">relative homology</a> <i id="mwXg">H</i><sub id="mwXw"><i id="mwYA">i</i></sub>(<i id="mwYQ">Y</i>, <i id="mwYg">S</i>). Under the same assumption on <i id="mwYw">X</i>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One-point_compactification" title="One-point compactification" class="mw-redirect" id="mwZA">one-point compactification</a> of <i id="mwZQ">X</i> is homeomorphic to a finite CW complex. As a result, Borel–Moore homology can be viewed as the relative homology of the one-point compactification with respect to the added point.</p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mwZg" aria-labelledby="Definition_via_Poincaré_duality"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Definition_via_Poincaré_duality"><span id="Definition_via_Poincar.C3.A9_duality" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Definition via Poincaré duality</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Borel%E2%80%93Moore_homology&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5" title="Edit section: Definition via Poincaré duality"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwZw">Let <i id="mwaA">X</i> be any locally compact space with a closed embedding into an oriented <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manifold" title="Manifold" id="mwaQ">manifold</a> <i id="mwag">M</i> of dimension <i id="mwaw">m</i>. Then</p>

<p id="mwbA"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-block" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt19" id="mwbQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{"display":"block"},"body":{"extsrc":"H^{BM}_i(X)= H^{m-i}(M,M\\setminus X),"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-display mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)=H^{m-i}(M,M\setminus X),}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msubsup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <msup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>m</mi>
            <mo>−<!-- − --></mo>
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>M</mi>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mi>M</mi>
        <mo class="MJX-variant">∖<!-- ∖ --></mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>,</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)=H^{m-i}(M,M\setminus X),}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/ba0844c9e2a0f5f95a1b95b77c3be461dfbfeec6" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-display mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.005ex; width:30.371ex; height:3.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)=H^{m-i}(M,M\setminus X),}"/></span></p>

<p id="mwbg">where in the right hand side, relative <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cohomology" title="Cohomology" id="mwbw">cohomology</a> is meant.<sup about="#mwt20" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-4"}}'><a href="#cite_note-4" id="mwcA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwcQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcg">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="6" id="mwdA" aria-labelledby="Definition_via_the_dualizing_complex"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Definition_via_the_dualizing_complex">Definition via the dualizing complex</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Borel%E2%80%93Moore_homology&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6" title="Edit section: Definition via the dualizing complex"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwdQ">For any locally compact space <i id="mwdg">X</i> of finite dimension, let <span class="texhtml " about="#mwt21" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwdw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"math","href":"./Template:Math"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"&apos;&apos;D&lt;sub>X&lt;/sub>&apos;&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'><i>D<sub>X</sub></i></span> be the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verdier_duality" title="Verdier duality" id="mweA">dualizing complex</a> of <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt22" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mweQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"X"}},"i":0}}]}'>X</span>. Then</p>

<p id="mweg"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-block" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt23" id="mwew" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{"display":"block"},"body":{"extsrc":"H^{BM}_i (X)=\\mathbb{H}^{-i} (X, D_X), "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-display mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)=\mathbb {H} ^{-i}(X,D_{X}),}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msubsup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">H</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo>−<!-- − --></mo>
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <msub>
          <mi>D</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>X</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>,</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)=\mathbb {H} ^{-i}(X,D_{X}),}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/f91d77cebb3d1ee04695fcfcef633aa7c524391e" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-display mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.005ex; width:25.111ex; height:3.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)=\mathbb {H} ^{-i}(X,D_{X}),}"/></span></p>

<p id="mwfA">where in the right hand side, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypercohomology" title="Hypercohomology" class="mw-redirect" id="mwfQ">hypercohomology</a> is meant.<sup about="#mwt24" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-5" id="mwfg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwfw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgA">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwgg" aria-labelledby="Properties"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Properties">Properties</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Borel%E2%80%93Moore_homology&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7" title="Edit section: Properties"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwgw">Borel−Moore homology is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Covariant_functor" title="Covariant functor" class="mw-redirect" id="mwhA">covariant functor</a> with respect to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proper_map" title="Proper map" id="mwhQ">proper maps</a>. That is, a proper map <i id="mwhg">f</i>: <i id="mwhw">X</i> → <i id="mwiA">Y</i> induces a <b id="mwiQ">pushforward</b> homomorphism <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt25" id="mwig" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H_i^{BM}(X) \\to H_i^{BM}(Y)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)\to H_{i}^{BM}(Y)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msubsup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
        <msubsup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>Y</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)\to H_{i}^{BM}(Y)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/cbde38b2dff4f5b2a7d41d3acbd6dc90edd0b49c" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.005ex; width:21.606ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)\to H_{i}^{BM}(Y)}"/></span> for all integers <i id="mwiw">i</i>. In contrast to ordinary homology, there is no pushforward on Borel−Moore homology for an arbitrary continuous map <i id="mwjA">f</i>. As a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Counterexample" title="Counterexample" id="mwjQ">counterexample</a>, one can consider the non-proper inclusion <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt26" id="mwjg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\R^2 \\setminus \\{0\\} \\to \\R^2."}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {R} ^{2}\setminus \{0\}\to \mathbb {R} ^{2}.}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">R</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>2</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo class="MJX-variant">∖<!-- ∖ --></mo>
        <mo fence="false" stretchy="false">{</mo>
        <mn>0</mn>
        <mo fence="false" stretchy="false">}</mo>
        <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">R</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mn>2</mn>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo>.</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {R} ^{2}\setminus \{0\}\to \mathbb {R} ^{2}.}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/9c8700a0c1834918a6de2c68a4e9e84ee0e71d06" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:15.408ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {R} ^{2}\setminus \{0\}\to \mathbb {R} ^{2}.}"/></span></p>

<p id="mwjw">Borel−Moore homology is a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contravariant_functor" title="Contravariant functor" class="mw-redirect" id="mwkA">contravariant functor</a> with respect to inclusions of open subsets. That is, for <i id="mwkQ">U</i> open in <i id="mwkg">X</i>, there is a natural <b id="mwkw">pullback</b> or <b id="mwlA">restriction</b> homomorphism <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt27" id="mwlQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"H_i^{BM}(X) \\to H_i^{BM}(U)."}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)\to H_{i}^{BM}(U).}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msubsup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo stretchy="false">→<!-- → --></mo>
        <msubsup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>U</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>.</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)\to H_{i}^{BM}(U).}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/7dd5534fc2008e5426e85946b16ae8127343d978" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.005ex; width:22.262ex; height:3.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{i}^{BM}(X)\to H_{i}^{BM}(U).}"/></span></p>

<p id="mwlg">For any locally compact space <i id="mwlw">X</i> and any closed subset <i id="mwmA">F</i>, with <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt28" id="mwmQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"U = X\\setminus F"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle U=X\setminus F}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>U</mi>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo class="MJX-variant">∖<!-- ∖ --></mo>
        <mi>F</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle U=X\setminus F}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/5d36e124e80ad93a477cd69fe513f14a4e4b9d16" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:10.797ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle U=X\setminus F}"/></span> the complement, there is a long exact <b id="mwmg">localization</b> sequence:<sup about="#mwt29" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-6" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-6" id="mwmw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwnA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwnQ">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwng">]</span></span></a></sup>
<span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-block" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt30" id="mwnw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{"display":"block"},"body":{"extsrc":" \\cdots \\to H^{BM}_i (F) \\to H^{BM}_i (X) \\to H^{BM}_i (U) \\to H^{BM}_{i-1} (F) \\to \\cdots "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-display mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="{\displaystyle \cdots \to H_{i}^{BM}(F)\to H_{i}^{BM}(X)\to H_{i}^{BM}(U)\to H_{i-1}^{BM}(F)\to \cdots }">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mo>⋯<!-- ⋯ --></mo>
