          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H^{i}(X){\stackrel {\cong }{\to }}H_{n-i}^{BM}(X)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/9954e27813922ff7acd3565121e05c7809e3f78d" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-display mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -1.171ex; width:18.115ex; height:4.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H^{i}(X){\stackrel {\cong }{\to }}H_{n-i}^{BM}(X)}"/></span>
for all integers <i id="mwrQ">i</i>. A different version of Poincaré duality for non-compact manifolds is the isomorphism from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cohomology_with_compact_support" title="Cohomology with compact support" id="mwrg">cohomology with compact support</a> to usual homology:
<span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-block" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt35" id="mwrw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{"display":"block"},"body":{"extsrc":"H^i_c(X) \\stackrel{\\cong}{\\to} H_{n-i}(X)."}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-display mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{c}^{i}(X){\stackrel {\cong }{\to }}H_{n-i}(X).}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msubsup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>c</mi>
