      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H_{c}^{i}(X){\stackrel {\cong }{\to }}H_{n-i}(X).}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/a7bcc8f07be7dcc721f3be8c51b24b5b03c9dbd2" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-display mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:18.448ex; height:3.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{c}^{i}(X){\stackrel {\cong }{\to }}H_{n-i}(X).}"/></span></p>

<p id="mwsA">A key advantage of Borel−Moore homology is that every <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orientable_manifold" title="Orientable manifold" class="mw-redirect" id="mwsQ">oriented manifold</a> <i id="mwsg">M</i> of dimension <i id="mwsw">n</i> (in particular, every <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smooth_scheme" title="Smooth scheme" id="mwtA">smooth</a> complex <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algebraic_variety" title="Algebraic variety" id="mwtQ">algebraic variety</a>), not necessarily compact, has a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fundamental_class" title="Fundamental class" id="mwtg">fundamental class</a> <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt38" id="mwtw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"[M] \\in H_n^{BM}(M)."}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle [M]\in H_{n}^{BM}(M).}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mo stretchy="false">[</mo>
        <mi>M</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">]</mo>
        <mo>∈<!-- ∈ --></mo>
        <msubsup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>M</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>.</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle [M]\in H_{n}^{BM}(M).}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/6c75b0066605c20f3c2ef0c69b3700165344c24a" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:16.785ex; height:3.009ex;" alt="{\displaystyle [M]\in H_{n}^{BM}(M).}"/></span> If the manifold <i id="mwuA">M</i> has a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triangulation_(topology)" title="Triangulation (topology)" id="mwuQ">triangulation</a>, then its fundamental class is represented by the sum of all the top dimensional simplices. In fact, in Borel−Moore homology, one can define a fundamental class for arbitrary (possibly singular) complex varieties. In this case the complement of the set of smooth points <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt39" id="mwug" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"M^{\\text{reg}} \\subset M"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle M^{\text{reg}}\subset M}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>M</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mtext>reg</mtext>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo>⊂<!-- ⊂ --></mo>
        <mi>M</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle M^{\text{reg}}\subset M}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/c5e874e9f80541d70b98097e218948152c558508" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:10.468ex; height:2.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle M^{\text{reg}}\subset M}"/></span> has (real) <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Codimension" title="Codimension" id="mwuw">codimension</a> at least 2, and by the long exact sequence above the top dimensional homologies of <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt36" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwvA" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"M"}},"i":0}}]}'>M</span> and <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt40" id="mwvQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"M^{\\text{reg}}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle M^{\text{reg}}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>M</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mtext>reg</mtext>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle M^{\text{reg}}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/edb8ca9eeec74d41a2a6db3622f7664df035d6c6" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:4.928ex; height:2.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle M^{\text{reg}}}"/></span> are canonically isomorphic. The fundamental class of <span class="texhtml mvar" style="font-style:italic;" about="#mwt37" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwvg" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"mvar","href":"./Template:Mvar"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"M"}},"i":0}}]}'>M</span> is then defined to be the fundamental class of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt41" id="mwvw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"M^{\\text{reg}}"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle M^{\text{reg}}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mi>M</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mtext>reg</mtext>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle M^{\text{reg}}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/edb8ca9eeec74d41a2a6db3622f7664df035d6c6" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:4.928ex; height:2.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle M^{\text{reg}}}"/></span>.<sup about="#mwt42" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-7"}}'><a href="#cite_note-7" id="mwwA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwwQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwwg">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwww">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="8" id="mwxA" aria-labelledby="Examples"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Examples">Examples</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Borel%E2%80%93Moore_homology&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8" title="Edit section: Examples"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="9" id="mwxQ" aria-labelledby="Compact_Spaces"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Compact_Spaces">Compact Spaces</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Borel%E2%80%93Moore_homology&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9" title="Edit section: Compact Spaces"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwxg">Given a compact topological space <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt43" id="mwxw" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"X"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle X}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>X</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle X}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/68baa052181f707c662844a465bfeeb135e82bab" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.98ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle X}"/></span> its Borel-Moore homology agrees with its standard homology; that is,</p>

<p id="mwyA"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-block" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt44" id="mwyQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{"display":"block"},"body":{"extsrc":"H^{BM}_*(X) \\cong H_*(X)"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-display mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{*}^{BM}(X)\cong H_{*}(X)}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msubsup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo>∗<!-- ∗ --></mo>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>≅<!-- ≅ --></mo>
        <msub>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo>∗<!-- ∗ --></mo>
          </mrow>
        </msub>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mi>X</mi>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H_{*}^{BM}(X)\cong H_{*}(X)}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/01bfe5113d44af0101ce88f91b3f98bfa97bc75d" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-display mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:18.972ex; height:3.009ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{*}^{BM}(X)\cong H_{*}(X)}"/></span></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="10" id="mwyg" aria-labelledby="Real_line"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Real_line">Real line</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Borel%E2%80%93Moore_homology&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10" title="Edit section: Real line"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwyw">The first non-trivial calculation of Borel-Moore homology is of the real line. First observe that any <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt45" id="mwzA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"0"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle 0}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mn>0</mn>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle 0}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/2aae8864a3c1fec9585261791a809ddec1489950" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.162ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle 0}"/></span>-chain is cohomologous to <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt46" id="mwzQ" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"0"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle 0}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mn>0</mn>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle 0}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/2aae8864a3c1fec9585261791a809ddec1489950" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:1.162ex; height:2.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle 0}"/></span>. Since this reduces to the case of a point <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt47" id="mwzg" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"p"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle p}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>p</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle p}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/81eac1e205430d1f40810df36a0edffdc367af36" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; margin-left: -0.089ex; width:1.259ex; height:2.009ex;" alt="{\displaystyle p}"/></span>, notice that we can take the Borel-Moore chain</p>

<p id="mwzw"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-block" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt48" id="mw0A" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{"display":"block"},"body":{"extsrc":"\\sigma = \\sum_{i=0}^\\infty 1\\cdot [p+i,p+i+1]"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-display mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="{\displaystyle \sigma =\sum _{i=0}^{\infty }1\cdot [p+i,p+i+1]}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>σ<!-- σ --></mi>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <munderover>
          <mo>∑<!-- ∑ --></mo>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>i</mi>
            <mo>=</mo>
            <mn>0</mn>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="normal">∞<!-- ∞ --></mi>
          </mrow>
        </munderover>
        <mn>1</mn>
        <mo>⋅<!-- ⋅ --></mo>
        <mo stretchy="false">[</mo>
        <mi>p</mi>
        <mo>+</mo>
        <mi>i</mi>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mi>p</mi>
        <mo>+</mo>
        <mi>i</mi>
        <mo>+</mo>
        <mn>1</mn>
        <mo stretchy="false">]</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \sigma =\sum _{i=0}^{\infty }1\cdot [p+i,p+i+1]}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/446ff8a55695d53aac90c9c17c6cee3d0ed56b40" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-display mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -3.005ex; width:26.967ex; height:6.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \sigma =\sum _{i=0}^{\infty }1\cdot [p+i,p+i+1]}"/></span></p>

<p id="mw0Q">since the boundary of this chain is <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt49" id="mw0g" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\partial\\sigma = p"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \partial \sigma =p}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi mathvariant="normal">∂<!-- ∂ --></mi>
        <mi>σ<!-- σ --></mi>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <mi>p</mi>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \partial \sigma =p}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/e4e11a5e28cd4f614914dbbcfb16548ad05a1530" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.671ex; width:6.916ex; height:2.509ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \partial \sigma =p}"/></span> and the non-existent point at infinity, the point is cohomologous to zero. Now, we can take the Borel-Moore chain</p>

<p id="mw0w"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-block" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt50" id="mw1A" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{"display":"block"},"body":{"extsrc":"\\sigma = \\sum_{-\\infty&lt;k&lt;\\infty} [k, k+1]"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-display mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="{\displaystyle \sigma =\sum _{-\infty &lt;k&lt;\infty }[k,k+1]}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <mi>σ<!-- σ --></mi>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <munder>
          <mo>∑<!-- ∑ --></mo>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mo>−<!-- − --></mo>
            <mi mathvariant="normal">∞<!-- ∞ --></mi>
            <mo>&lt;</mo>
            <mi>k</mi>
            <mo>&lt;</mo>
            <mi mathvariant="normal">∞<!-- ∞ --></mi>
          </mrow>
        </munder>
        <mo stretchy="false">[</mo>
        <mi>k</mi>
        <mo>,</mo>
        <mi>k</mi>
        <mo>+</mo>
        <mn>1</mn>
        <mo stretchy="false">]</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \sigma =\sum _{-\infty &lt;k&lt;\infty }[k,k+1]}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/cfbcd45625edf74b7df9051f441729bcbb7a6d5e" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-display mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -3.171ex; width:21.159ex; height:5.676ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \sigma =\sum _{-\infty &lt;k&lt;\infty }[k,k+1]}"/></span></p>

<p id="mw1Q">which has no boundary, hence is a homology class. This shows that</p>

<p id="mw1g"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-block" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt51" id="mw1w" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{"display":"block"},"body":{"extsrc":" H_k^{BM}(\\R) = \\begin{cases} \\Z &amp; k = 1 \\\\ 0 &amp; \\text{otherwise} \\end{cases} "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-display mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{k}^{BM}(\mathbb {R} )={\begin{cases}\mathbb {Z} &amp;k=1\\0&amp;{\text{otherwise}}\end{cases}}}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msubsup>
          <mi>H</mi>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>k</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>B</mi>
            <mi>M</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msubsup>
        <mo stretchy="false">(</mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mi mathvariant="double-struck">R</mi>
        </mrow>
        <mo stretchy="false">)</mo>
        <mo>=</mo>
        <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
          <mrow>
            <mo>{</mo>
            <mtable columnalign="left left" rowspacing=".2em" columnspacing="1em" displaystyle="false">
              <mtr>
                <mtd>
                  <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
                    <mi mathvariant="double-struck">Z</mi>
                  </mrow>
                </mtd>
                <mtd>
                  <mi>k</mi>
                  <mo>=</mo>
                  <mn>1</mn>
                </mtd>
              </mtr>
              <mtr>
                <mtd>
                  <mn>0</mn>
                </mtd>
                <mtd>
                  <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
                    <mtext>otherwise</mtext>
                  </mrow>
                </mtd>
              </mtr>
            </mtable>
            <mo fence="true" stretchy="true" symmetric="true"></mo>
          </mrow>
        </mrow>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle H_{k}^{BM}(\mathbb {R} )={\begin{cases}\mathbb {Z} &amp;k=1\\0&amp;{\text{otherwise}}\end{cases}}}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/0bfa0b44f2afce371c2955cf411fdce77dbbbabe" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-display mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -2.505ex; width:27.84ex; height:6.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{k}^{BM}(\mathbb {R} )={\begin{cases}\mathbb {Z} &amp;k=1\\0&amp;{\text{otherwise}}\end{cases}}}"/></span></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="11" id="mw2A" aria-labelledby="Real_n-space"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Real_n-space">Real n-space</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Borel%E2%80%93Moore_homology&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11" title="Edit section: Real n-space"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mw2Q">The previous computation can be generalized to the case <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt52" id="mw2g" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"\\R^n."}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle \mathbb {R} ^{n}.}">
  <semantics>
    <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
      <mstyle displaystyle="true" scriptlevel="0">
        <msup>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi mathvariant="double-struck">R</mi>
          </mrow>
          <mrow class="MJX-TeXAtom-ORD">
            <mi>n</mi>
          </mrow>
        </msup>
        <mo>.</mo>
      </mstyle>
    </mrow>
    <annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\displaystyle \mathbb {R} ^{n}.}</annotation>
  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/76ef548febfc9981762740107858be9e3a5576c3" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.338ex; width:3.543ex; height:2.343ex;" alt="{\displaystyle \mathbb {R} ^{n}.}"/></span> We get</p>

<p id="mw2w"><span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-block" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt53" id="mw3A" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{"display":"block"},"body":{"extsrc":" H_k^{BM}(\\R^n) = \\begin{cases} \\Z &amp; k = n \\\\ 0 &amp; \\text{otherwise} \\end{cases} "}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-display mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" alttext="{\displaystyle H_{k}^{BM}(\mathbb {R} ^{n})={\begin{cases}\mathbb {Z} &amp;k=n\\0&amp;{\text{otherwise}}\end{cases}}}">
  <semantics>
