  </semantics>
</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/611f82680c9bfe2e833a2bf6f9a04518db287b48" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-display mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -2.505ex; width:29.059ex; height:6.176ex;" alt="{\displaystyle H_{k}^{BM}(\mathbb {R} ^{n})={\begin{cases}\mathbb {Z} &amp;k=n\\0&amp;{\text{otherwise}}\end{cases}}}"/></span></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="12" id="mw3Q" aria-labelledby="Infinite_Cylinder"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Infinite_Cylinder">Infinite Cylinder</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Borel%E2%80%93Moore_homology&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12" title="Edit section: Infinite Cylinder"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mw3g">Using the Künneth decomposition, we can see that the infinite cylinder <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt54" id="mw3w" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"S^1\\times\\R"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle S^{1}\times \mathbb {R} }">
  <semantics>
